  },
  {
   "id": "b274",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Mate.",
   "directed": "[short pause] Mate."
  },
  {
   "id": "b275",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The very reality in which the object appears is already complete.",
   "directed": "The very reality in which the object appears is already complete."
  },
  {
   "id": "b276",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "What are you looking for outside it?",
   "directed": "What are you looking for outside it?"
  },
  {
   "id": "b277",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Fourth: Samāna — everything comes together\nNow we get samāna.",
   "directed": "Fourth: Samāna — everything comes together\nNow we get samāna."
  },
  {
   "id": "b278",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The equalising vital energy.",
   "directed": "The equalising vital energy."
  },
  {
   "id": "b279",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And with its arising, the practitioner experiences:",
   "directed": "[short pause] And with its arising, the practitioner experiences:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b280",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Saṅghaṭṭa-viśrānti.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Saṅghaṭṭa-viśrānti."
  },
  {
   "id": "b281",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Repose in conjunction.",
   "directed": "Repose in conjunction."
  },
  {
   "id": "b282",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The coming together of movements previously experienced as distinct.",
   "directed": "The coming together of movements previously experienced as distinct."
  },
  {
   "id": "b283",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Outward and inward.",
   "directed": "Outward and inward."
  },
  {
   "id": "b284",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Subject and object.",
   "directed": "Subject and object."
  },
  {
   "id": "b285",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The apparent division begins to settle.",
   "directed": "The apparent division begins to settle."
  },
  {
   "id": "b286",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now remember the fire-wheel?",
   "directed": "Now remember the fire-wheel?"
  },
  {
   "id": "b287",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Remember how we brought the knower, knowing and known into conjunction?",
   "directed": "Remember how we brought the knower, knowing and known into conjunction?"
  },
  {
   "id": "b288",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "We’re approaching that same recognition through another support.",
   "directed": "We’re approaching that same recognition through another support."
  },
  {
   "id": "b289",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not imaginative visualisation this time.",
   "directed": "Not imaginative visualisation this time."
  },
  {
   "id": "b290",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Vital energy.",
   "directed": "Vital energy."
  },
  {
   "id": "b291",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And now something rather dramatic happens.",
   "directed": "And now something rather dramatic happens."
  },
  {
   "id": "b292",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Fifth: Udāna — the fire devours the whole operation\nHere comes udāna.",
   "directed": "Fifth: Udāna — the fire devours the whole operation\nHere comes udāna."
  },
  {
   "id": "b293",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The ascending vital energy.",
   "directed": "The ascending vital energy."
  },
  {
   "id": "b294",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And Abhinavagupta associates it with fire.",
   "directed": "And Abhinavagupta associates it with fire."
  },
  {
   "id": "b295",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Udāna-vahni.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Udāna-vahni."
  },
  {
   "id": "b296",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now this fire doesn’t merely dissolve a particular object.",
   "directed": "Now this fire doesn’t merely dissolve a particular object."
  },
  {
   "id": "b297",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "It consumes the very divisions through which cognition occurs.",
   "directed": "It consumes the very divisions through which cognition occurs."
  },
  {
   "id": "b298",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The knower.",
   "directed": "The knower."
  },
  {
   "id": "b299",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The known.",
   "directed": "The known."
  },
  {
   "id": "b300",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The operations by which the known is apprehended.",
   "directed": "The operations by which the known is apprehended."
  },
  {
   "id": "b301",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Mātṛ-meyādi-kalanā.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Mātṛ-meyādi-kalanā."
  },
  {
   "id": "b302",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "All swallowed.",
   "directed": "All swallowed."
  },
  {
   "id": "b303",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And don’t imagine that this means the universe must physically vanish.",
   "directed": "And don’t imagine that this means the universe must physically vanish."
  },
  {
   "id": "b304",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The point is the dissolution of these divisions as independently existing realities.",
   "directed": "The point is the dissolution of these divisions as independently existing realities."
  },
  {
   "id": "b305",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The subject is not standing apart from consciousness.",
   "directed": "The subject is not standing apart from consciousness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b306",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The object is not standing apart from consciousness.",
   "directed": "The object is not standing apart from consciousness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b307",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The very act of knowing is not standing apart from consciousness.",
   "directed": "The very act of knowing is not standing apart from consciousness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b308",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The fire of udāna devours their supposed separateness.",
   "directed": "The fire of udāna devours their supposed separateness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b309",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And then the fire itself subsides.",
   "directed": "And then the fire itself subsides."
  },
  {
   "id": "b310",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "What remains?",
   "directed": "What remains?"
  },
  {
   "id": "b311",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Sixth: Vyāna — consciousness everywhere\nVyāna.",
   "directed": "Sixth: Vyāna — consciousness everywhere\nVyāna."
  },
  {
   "id": "b312",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The pervasive vital energy.",
   "directed": "The pervasive vital energy."
  },
  {
   "id": "b313",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now the limitations through which consciousness appeared restricted no longer define the experience.",
   "directed": "Now the limitations through which consciousness appeared restricted no longer define the experience."
  },
  {
   "id": "b314",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Sarvāvaccheda-vandhya.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Sarvāvaccheda-vandhya."
  },
  {
   "id": "b315",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Free from all delimitation.",
   "directed": "Free from all delimitation."
  },
  {
   "id": "b316",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And Abhinavagupta uses a lovely verb here.",
   "directed": "And Abhinavagupta uses a lovely verb here."
  },
  {
   "id": "b317",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Sphurati.",
   "directed": "Sphurati."
  },
  {
   "id": "b318",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "It flashes.",
   "directed": "It flashes."
  },
  {
   "id": "b319",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "It shines.",
   "directed": "It shines."
  },
  {
   "id": "b320",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "It vibrates.",
   "directed": "It vibrates."
  },
  {
   "id": "b321",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Consciousness shines forth unrestricted by those divisions.",
   "directed": "Consciousness shines forth unrestricted by those divisions."
  },
  {
   "id": "b322",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not sitting in one corner of the body like a little spectator.",
   "directed": "Not sitting in one corner of the body like a little spectator."
  },
  {
   "id": "b323",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not trapped in some tiny mental chamber.",
   "directed": "Not trapped in some tiny mental chamber."
  },
  {
   "id": "b324",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But apprehended as the all-pervasive reality.",
   "directed": "But apprehended as the all-pervasive reality."
  },
  {
   "id": "b325",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The movement began in the Heart, extended toward the world, returned inward, united its divisions, dissolved them, and culminated in unrestricted awareness.",
   "directed": "The movement began in the Heart, extended toward the world, returned inward, united its divisions, dissolved them, and culminated in unrestricted awareness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b326",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And now you might ask:",
   "directed": "[short pause] And now you might ask:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b327",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "man",
   "text": "“Abhinava, mate, what does any of this actually feel like?”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “Abhinava, mate, what does any of this actually feel like?”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b328",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Excellent question.",
   "directed": "Excellent question."
  },
  {
   "id": "b329",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Because apparently there are six kinds of bliss involved.",
   "directed": "Because apparently there are six kinds of bliss involved."
  },
  {
   "id": "b330",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And I know what you’re thinking.",
   "directed": "And I know what you’re thinking."
  },
  {
   "id": "b331",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Six?",
   "directed": "Six?"
  },
  {
   "id": "b332",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Bloody hell.",
   "directed": "Bloody hell."
  },
  {
   "id": "b333",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "We’re going to need a bigger vocabulary.",
   "directed": "We’re going to need a bigger vocabulary."
  },
  {
   "id": "b334",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "6. The six levels of bliss\nHere they are.",
   "directed": "6. The six levels of bliss\nHere they are."
  },
  {
   "id": "b335",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Nijānanda.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Nijānanda."
  },
  {
   "id": "b336",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The bliss of one’s own nature.",
   "directed": "The bliss of one’s own nature."
  },
  {
   "id": "b337",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Associated with the original repose in the Heart’s openness.",
   "directed": "Associated with the original repose in the Heart’s openness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b338",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Nija means one’s own, intrinsic, belonging to oneself.",
   "directed": "Nija means one’s own, intrinsic, belonging to oneself."
  },
  {
   "id": "b339",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "So nijānanda is the bliss inherent in one’s own being.",
   "directed": "So nijānanda is the bliss inherent in one’s own being."
  },
  {
   "id": "b340",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "No external object required.",
   "directed": "No external object required."
  },
  {
   "id": "b341",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Not a pleasure supplied from somewhere else.",
   "directed": "Not a pleasure supplied from somewhere else."
  },
  {
   "id": "b342",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The bliss of what you are.",
   "directed": "The bliss of what you are."
  },
  {
   "id": "b343",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Nirānanda.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Nirānanda."
  },
  {
   "id": "b344",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Now, this one’s interesting because the prefix nir- ordinarily suggests absence or freedom from.",
   "directed": "Now, this one’s interesting because the prefix nir- ordinarily suggests absence or freedom from."
  },
  {
   "id": "b345",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "So you might think:",
   "directed": "[short pause] So you might think:"
  },
  {
   "id": "b346",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "dialogue",
   "voice": "man",
   "text": "“Hang on, is this the bliss of having no bliss?”",
   "directed": "[short pause] “Hang on, is this the bliss of having no bliss?”"
  },
  {
   "id": "b347",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Don’t be ridiculous.",
   "directed": "Don’t be ridiculous."
  },
  {
   "id": "b348",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "We’re not constructing an ordinary English compound.",
   "directed": "We’re not constructing an ordinary English compound."
  },
  {
   "id": "b349",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "This is a technical name for the repose associated with the outward prāṇa movement.",
   "directed": "This is a technical name for the repose associated with the outward prāṇa movement."
  },
  {
   "id": "b350",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The character of bliss is changing as consciousness moves into manifestation.",
   "directed": "The character of bliss is changing as consciousness moves into manifestation."
  },
  {
   "id": "b351",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Parānanda.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Parānanda."
  },
  {
   "id": "b352",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The bliss of the other, or the bliss associated with what appears beyond oneself.",
   "directed": "The bliss of the other, or the bliss associated with what appears beyond oneself."
  },
  {
   "id": "b353",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "This belongs to the movement of apāna.",
   "directed": "This belongs to the movement of apāna."
  },
  {
   "id": "b354",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "And here’s the paradox.",
   "directed": "And here’s the paradox."
  },
  {
   "id": "b355",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The apparent other is being drawn into the fullness of one’s own consciousness.",
   "directed": "The apparent other is being drawn into the fullness of one’s own consciousness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b356",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "So what initially appeared external becomes apprehended within the Self.",
   "directed": "So what initially appeared external becomes apprehended within the Self."
  },
  {
   "id": "b357",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Brahmānanda.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Brahmānanda."
  },
  {
   "id": "b358",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The bliss of expansive fullness.",
   "directed": "The bliss of expansive fullness."
  },
  {
   "id": "b359",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Associated here with samāna and the conjunction of previously differentiated movements.",
   "directed": "Associated here with samāna and the conjunction of previously differentiated movements."
  },
  {
   "id": "b360",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "The word brahman carries the sense of vastness or expansion in its etymological background.",
   "directed": "The word brahman carries the sense of vastness or expansion in its etymological background."
  },
  {
   "id": "b361",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "So there’s a magnificent sense of fullness here.",
   "directed": "So there’s a magnificent sense of fullness here."
  },
  {
   "id": "b362",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "But don’t confuse this technical stage with the unrestricted absolute itself.",
   "directed": "But don’t confuse this technical stage with the unrestricted absolute itself."
  },
  {
   "id": "b363",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "We’re still discussing a particular repose within this practice.",
   "directed": "We’re still discussing a particular repose within this practice."
  },
  {
   "id": "b364",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "verse",
   "voice": "verse",
   "text": "Mahānanda.",
   "directed": "[slowly] Mahānanda."
  },
  {
   "id": "b365",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Great bliss.",
   "directed": "Great bliss."
  },
  {
   "id": "b366",
   "section": "Tantrasāra — Chapter 5",
   "type": "narration",
   "voice": "granny",
   "text": "Mahā — great.",
   "directed": "Mahā — great."
  },
  {
   "id": "b367",
